# Release-only additions for the UNISOC SL8541E watches. Apply AFTER watch_hardening.fragment.
# These remove development and measurement facilities that are used while bringing the
# kernel up (and by the project's measurement tooling), so do not use for dev builds.
# NOT READY: only use after the SELinux policy is fixed for enforcing and a release build
# has booted with all services and vendor HALs checked on each device.

# debugfs exposes driver internals (and some writable knobs) to root. AOSP 8.1 does not need it;
# vendor HALs/daemons that read debugfs are not checked yet, so verify them on the device.
# CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is not set
# Kernel tracing (ftrace, events, atrace). Reduces attack surface and kernel size. atrace/systrace stop working.
# CONFIG_FTRACE is not set
# Only symbols for functions (not data) in /proc/kallsyms (kptr_restrict still applies).
# CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL is not set
# SLUB red zones/poisoning on every cache by default: heavy CPU/memory cost on a watch.
# CONFIG_SLUB_DEBUG_ON is not set
# CONFIG_SLUB_STATS is not set
# Enforcing SELinux cannot be switched to permissive at runtime or by cmdline; the DM63
# currently runs Permissive, so check policy denials before shipping this.
# CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_DEVELOP is not set
